==============================================================================
PART B -- THE HAM-PATH TRICK: fibres without touching the 2^m cube
==============================================================================
 fibre(c) <-> HamPaths(T_c)/Aut(T_c)  (Aut acts freely on Ham paths, canon LEM-003)
 so |fibre(c)| = H(c)/|Aut(c)| -- and the fibre ITSELF is enumerable from one rep.

 n=4: classes=4 (A000568)  SC=2  merged=3  G_n edges=5
   checksum sum H/|Aut| = 8  vs 2^m = 8 : True   [agrees with exhaustive: True]
   cost: 24 canonicalisations, 0.0s   vs naive 2^C(n,2) = 64 tournaments

 n=5: classes=12 (A000568)  SC=8  merged=10  G_n edges=30
   checksum sum H/|Aut| = 64  vs 2^m = 64 : True   [agrees with exhaustive: True]
   cost: 120 canonicalisations, 0.0s   vs naive 2^C(n,2) = 1024 tournaments

 n=6: classes=56 (A000568)  SC=12  merged=34  G_n edges=290
   checksum sum H/|Aut| = 1024  vs 2^m = 1024 : True   [agrees with exhaustive: True]
   cost: 840 canonicalisations, 0.0s   vs naive 2^C(n,2) = 32768 tournaments

 n=7: classes=456 (A000568)  SC=88  merged=272  G_n edges=4086
   checksum sum H/|Aut| = 32768  vs 2^m = 32768 : True   [agrees with exhaustive: n/a]
   cost: 9576 canonicalisations, 0.6s   vs naive 2^C(n,2) = 2097152 tournaments

